{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/800734-sell-me-on-changeling","id":800734,"title":"Sell me on Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-04T14:16:00-08:00","id":800734,"title":"Sell me on Changeling","content":"Evenign all. i been exploring the world of darkness for a number of years now.<br /> Im aware of how popular changeling is, i recently got a copy of the corebook and player's guide. i been trying to Understand it but theres some things that just dont Click on me.<br /> <br /> my experience in the WoD mainly composes Vampire, Werewolf, Hunter, Mage , Demon and Wraith. So, sell me on changeling.<br /> <br /> i been told that under his colours, it lies within a very grim and pretty dark game.<br /> <br /> Please, convince me to explore a bit more further, both on plot and mechanics","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T02:29:23-08:00","id":801236,"title":"","content":"Well it's a game that allows you to play The Chronicles of Narnia, The Dresden Files, Pan's Labyrinth, Hellboy, Harry Potter, Neverwhere and Legend if you want. It's the most versatile game in the World of Darkness for playing urban fantasy, and if you play a game set in the Dreaming, you can play just about any fantasy game too.<br /> <br /> Like Demon, you're a being who once had great power, now trapped in a human body, surrounded by people who don't know what you are. If you believe the fae, they're actually the ones who shaped the world in the early days. In many ways, CTD was an early prototype for DTF.<br /> <br /> Any monster can be created as a chimera. It's easy enough to create a kith that allows you to play whatever critter you want, too.<br /> <br /> As a character, you have access to a whole hidden world of magic and secrets. It's great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T09:43:56-08:00","id":801458,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition\">We had this thread a few weeks ago, hadn't we?</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling the Dreaming is a game where your character (we'll call him Steve) opens his eyes one day and realises that he's not an office worker at Jobson and Co, but rather that he's a magical prince from the dreamland of Arcadia, with mystic powers and ancient romance and all that, and that his boss isn't really Mr. Jobson, the middle manager in third generation, but rather an evil alien monster that came to our world to eat Imagination and promote Soul Crushing Despair of Office Life. So Steve takes his Sword of Glory (which boring muggles see as his old golf club) and goes on to slay dragons and beat Mr. Jobson to death or something. And then you go and have a creepy romance with a Sidhe princess in the body of a ten year old girl.<br /> <br /> Also Tony Diterlizzi's art is pretty good.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T07:49:30-08:00","id":802100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/800734-sell-me-on-changeling?p=801458#post801458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/783480-sell-me-on-changeling-the-dreaming-20th-anniversary-edition\">We had this thread a few weeks ago, hadn't we?</a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's...quite the uncharitable portrayal of the game. And inaccurate, in that there's no &quot;realizing he's not an office worker at Jobson and Co.,&quot; because he IS. He is <i>also</i> a magic faerie prince. Mr. Jobson might be an evil dream-devouring monster in addition to being Mr. Jobson, his boss, but it is unlikely that Stephan Goldensword's assault on Jormsongandr the Vile will look like Steve hitting Mr. Jobson with a golf club. It's more probable that the mortal office workers will see them arguing, with Steve jabbing pointedly with a pen or marker and possibly wielding papers showing stock prices and financial records like shields. The Dreaming sees an epic sword fight between the heroic prince and the revealed dragon. When Steve wins his conflict, a defeated Mr. Jobson may change his ways or even retire, while the evil Dragon is slain. Steve may even become the new manager as the Prince assumes his throne. Or maybe he'll just move on to a new job as the Prince rides into the sunset.<br /> <br /> As for the creepy romance with a 10-year-old Sidhe Queen... that's not really promoted by Changeling: the Dreaming, but it's no more discouraged there than in any other game. You could make an interesting drama around the stress of it, if you had some sort of past-life connection between the fae souls involved now having to figure out how to deal with this incredibly awkward age difference. But if you came up with that, any squick is on you; it's not really introduced nor invited by the game in any direct sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T08:07:07-08:00","id":802105,"title":"","content":"I'm having this same issue, I've only had experience with VtM so I don't have as much knowledge as OP. The Changeling game sounds right up my alley but when I read the rulebook my eyes crossed. I just cannot understand how the hell to make a character. Does anyone have a simplified version of it? Or at least a way to explain it like I'm an idiot because apparently I am. I want to play so bad but I cannot click with the character creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T09:00:35-08:00","id":802145,"title":"","content":"Where do you get lost in it? The rules for chargen seem fairly straight-forward to me: so many dots for Attributes, so many for Abilities, so many for Backgrounds, Arts, and Realms. Freebies for merits/flaws and more dots in areas you feel need shoring up.<br /> <br /> Is it some aspect of interactions you don't get? I'm not trying to be obtuse, here, just trying to figure out what's confusing you. There are a lot of possible places for confusion to arise, so it's easier to focus on the specific ones causing difficulty than to try to scattershot and nail them all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T09:06:20-08:00","id":802148,"title":"","content":"Oh, you know what I just realized? We were working with Changeling: The Lost. This was a couple months ago so I had forgotten it wasn't Dreaming. Yeah, Lost confused me, I haven't taken a look at Dreaming yet. But if it's like you say Segev then it's not as confusing as Lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T09:08:28-08:00","id":802150,"title":"","content":"I read Lost, but I don't recall it, as I never tried to build a PC. So I can't comment usefully, sorry. Good luck!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T09:13:20-08:00","id":802154,"title":"","content":"No problem, based on what you say I may get Dreaming because it sounds way easier than Lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T09:20:54-08:00","id":802160,"title":"","content":"Of all the nWoD vs oWoD splats, Changeling changed the most, in my opinion. So much so that the very premise is nigh unrecognizable.<br /> <br /> I like both, in theory, though I like the Dreaming better for nostalgic reasons. (Also, I may *ahem* prefer to play one of the exiled Fae than an escaped mortal, if I ever play in a Lost game. I need to get the book with their rules.)<br /> <br /> In the Dreaming, Changelings are immortal faerie souls grafted onto and sharing a body with mortal humans, a process which happens as the mortal is born, forming a unique being with mortal concerns and immortal memories and powers. The memories tend to be fuzzy, though, unless you take certain merits/backgrounds. It's mostly a game about playing a magical creature of surreality and myth in a world whose very normalcy is literally painful and destructive to them, and sheltering, therefore, your mythic nature behind a mask of your own normalcy. It's a game of conflicting needs, existing simultaneously in two overlapping worlds, and having to reconcile it all together. The presentation in the extant books is rather Childling/growing-up centric, though I personally think there's potential in different kinds of foci for the stories of young adult and older Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T16:31:52-08:00","id":802432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/800734-sell-me-on-changeling?p=802100#post802100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the creepy romance with a 10-year-old Sidhe Queen... that's not really promoted by Changeling: the Dreaming, but it's no more discouraged there than in any other game. You could make an interesting drama around the stress of it, if you had some sort of past-life connection between the fae souls involved now having to figure out how to deal with this incredibly awkward age difference. But if you came up with that, any squick is on you; it's not really introduced nor invited by the game in any direct sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm extremely creeped out by the fact that you support this romance. And the game does in fact introduce and invite this kind of thing by having &quot;a 3-13 year old with a thousand years old memories&quot; as one of the three core subtypes. It further makes things worse by allowing you to play a childling satyr who can inspire carnal passion in people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T17:27:47-08:00","id":802475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/800734-sell-me-on-changeling?p=802432#post802432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm extremely creeped out by the fact that you support this romance. And the game does in fact introduce and invite this kind of thing by having &amp;quot;a 3-13 year old with a thousand years old memories&amp;quot; as one of the three core subtypes. It further makes things worse by allowing you to play a childling satyr who can inspire carnal passion in people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because you can doesn't mean you should. In theory, Vampire allows for thousand-year old Lolitas to seduce older people, too. I'm pretty sure that any game can allow for inappropriate relations in the hands of the wrong players, unless said game specifically restricts players to specific age ranges.<br /> <br /> You also have to remember that changelings are part human too, so the human morality that stops the average person engaging in such relationships will be something they've grown up with too. <br /> <br /> Most changelings chrysalise around puberty anyway, by which point they know, having lived as humans for years, to keep away from creeps. This won't disappear the second they begin to see chimerical reality.<br /> <br /> Changelings are aware of the delicate balancing act between mortal and chimerical life, and this is one of those situations where their mortal lives would probably give them serious reservations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T05:26:46-08:00","id":802992,"title":"","content":"Supporting the mechanics existing and actually doing it are completely different things. And with the right player, ie one that isn't just forcing their creepy fetishes on others, I think a character of that type could be played dramatically well. It's not a new idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T06:43:22-08:00","id":803041,"title":"","content":"Yeah, sorry, ANY game involving &quot;ancient memories&quot; or &quot;ageless immortals&quot; <i>can</i> be used to explore this in creepy, dramatic, fetishistic, or any of a variety of ways, ranging in levels of acceptability and squick depending on handling, audience, and maturity (and I don't just mean &quot;old enough to watch porn&quot;) of the gamers. Saying it's &quot;invited&quot; because of this, and therefore the game is bad/wrong/evil, is essentially saying that you can't have anything involving immortality in your gameline. Because a teen-looking immortal is ALSO so-old-that-it-is-creepy if she romances an apparent peer, and a 30-year-old vampires who was turned 16 years ago is probably going to find her mortal paramores of approximately her age (or even several years her junior) being seen as &quot;creepy&quot; for hitting on that &quot;young girl.&quot; Heck, imagine the &quot;forbidden love&quot; angle between a werewolf and a vampire, with both falling in love in their mid-teens and staying together even after she was turned and he discovered his nature. By the time they're 40, he looks like a creeper for being with his love.<br /> <br /> The point being, the game lines don't explicitly call for any of this. You can go there, however, because age being deceptive is a theme of the games.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the satyr childling, the context does imply that the satyr's power is used for carnal lust front-and-center, but it doesn't state outright that that's all it can be used for, and in fact lists it as only one of several options. A satyr childling may NOT evoke such things; he might, instead, drive people to fits of childish passion and letting go of their straight-laced &quot;grown-up&quot; inhibitions to just have fun and play games and be silly. There's more to inhibition than sex, after all. I will agree that the focus on satyr sensuality means that it's natural to go &quot;wait a moment...&quot; if you try to play a satyr childling, but asserting that it's the intent and the primary way to go is looking for an excuse to be offended. Or to be creepy, though obviously if one is holding it out as a reason the game is creepy, one is not likely to try to JUSTIFY one's own creepiness with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T06:48:37-08:00","id":803048,"title":"","content":"I actually like the idea of the satyr making everyone around them act like a shameless child, sounds like a fun character to play. Just random games of tag breaking out in the middle of an office, that'd be awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T07:52:30-08:00","id":803085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/800734-sell-me-on-changeling?p=803041#post803041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the satyr childling, the context does imply that the satyr's power is used for carnal lust front-and-center, but it doesn't state outright that that's all it can be used for, and in fact lists it as only one of several options. A satyr childling may NOT evoke such things; he might, instead, drive people to fits of childish passion and letting go of their straight-laced &quot;grown-up&quot; inhibitions to just have fun and play games and be silly. There's more to inhibition than sex, after all. I will agree that the focus on satyr sensuality means that it's natural to go &quot;wait a moment...&quot; if you try to play a satyr childling, but asserting that it's the intent and the primary way to go is looking for an excuse to be offended. Or to be creepy, though obviously if one is holding it out as a reason the game is creepy, one is not likely to try to JUSTIFY one's own creepiness with it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Changeling the Dreaming</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gift of Pan - Dionysian revelry is high ritual to these fae. Singing, music, and dance can be used to stir fae and mortals alike to the height of carnal passion. Anyone who fails a Willpower roll (difficulty 7) is swept away by hidden desires and the activity of the evening.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand why you'd mind caulk away all the horrible implications of the fuckmusic Satyrs have. But &quot;carnal passion&quot; in english means one thing and one thing only 99% of the time. Satyrs also possess a number of merits and flaws that revolve specifically around sex, so yes, the writers do mean sex when they say &quot;carnal passion&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T08:40:24-08:00","id":803118,"title":"","content":"Carnal passion can mean anything you want it to mean as far as the game goes. It's the player's/storyteller's decision. Yes, it can be used to mean sexual desires and whatnot, and it is most of the time. We're not arguing that, but if you want to play the character differently there's nothing stopping you, that's the beauty of these games, you have freedom as to how the rules are interpreted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T09:22:30-08:00","id":803152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/800734-sell-me-on-changeling?p=803085#post803085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I understand why you'd mind caulk away all the horrible implications of the fuckmusic Satyrs have. But &quot;carnal passion&quot; in english means one thing and one thing only 99% of the time. Satyrs also possess a number of merits and flaws that revolve specifically around sex, so yes, the writers do mean sex when they say &quot;carnal passion&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, &quot;carnal passion&quot; isn't the only thing they inspire. And again, you're the one bringing Childlings into it. I do not, in any way, deny that the writers were thinking &quot;sex&quot; when they wrote a lot of that. I do suspect that they were thinking &quot;Wilders&quot; and didn't stop to consider &quot;Childlings&quot; much if at all. Thorough, well-thought-out rules are not something C:tD is known for. Sadly.<br /> <br /> Given that there ARE options that are not &quot;wild and crazy sex&quot; to go with, insisting that it MUST conflate children with it is insisting on squick that is not necessary and certainly is not overtly encouraged. You have to stop and think about it a moment to find it, and you CAN avoid it with equally careful thought.<br /> <br /> So why are we being hung up on this in a thread meant to sell somebody on a game? Is it to threadcrap and hate on the game, or is it just to be hung up on this subject?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T09:48:59-08:00","id":803171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/800734-sell-me-on-changeling?p=803152#post803152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that there ARE options that are not &quot;wild and crazy sex&quot; to go with, insisting that it MUST conflate children with it is insisting on squick that is not necessary and certainly is not overtly encouraged. You have to stop and think about it a moment to find it, and you CAN avoid it with equally careful thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>What options? Gift of Pan does one thing, and one thing only - stir people to the height of carnal passion. I gave you the quote from the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So why are we being hung up on this in a thread meant to sell somebody on a game? Is it to threadcrap and hate on the game, or is it just to be hung up on this subject? </div> </div> </div>Because a 20th anniversary edition is being written, which means the flaws in the game can be identified and fixed. And &quot;loli sex goddes&quot; as one of the core character archetypes is definitely a massive flaw in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T10:01:08-08:00","id":803177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/800734-sell-me-on-changeling?p=803171#post803171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What options? Gift of Pan does one thing, and one thing only - stir people to the height of carnal passion. I gave you the quote from the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to look it up for context. Though I can still say with confidence that the writers were thinking &quot;Wilders&quot; when they wrote it. And that &quot;childling&quot; didn't cross their minds.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/800734-sell-me-on-changeling?p=803171#post803171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because a 20th anniversary edition is being written, which means the flaws in the game can be identified and fixed. And &quot;loli sex goddes&quot; as one of the core character archetypes is definitely a massive flaw in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree that it would be nice to have some language giving satyr childling ideas that define other things as their potential concepts, I do not think that is a &quot;core archetype,&quot; because it isn't presented as such. It's an archetype that can arise from a natural combination of things in the game, certainly, and do so easily, but a &quot;core archetype&quot; is generally more front-and-center and not left to be &quot;discovered&quot; amongst combinations of things that are possible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T13:16:58-08:00","id":803311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/800734-sell-me-on-changeling?p=803171#post803171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because a 20th anniversary edition is being written, which means the flaws in the game can be identified and fixed. And &quot;loli sex goddes&quot; as one of the core character archetypes is definitely a massive flaw in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, you treat the matter as if it was new and recently noticed thing. It is not, people have been aware of the issues related to childlings for years. That, and the way you focus on that aspect and the language you use regarding it is presenting the issue as if it was a common thing in Changeling.<br /> <br /> This is not the case, remember that most Changeling players are used to taking stuff they like and ignoring the rest. Or dealing with conflicting rules vs lore the setting presents. Any online game with CtD will be chock full of houserules, almost on princible. So any loli sex goddess would be houseruled away before it would even cross anyone's mind.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T13:57:57-08:00","id":803344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/800734-sell-me-on-changeling?p=803311#post803311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is, you treat the matter as if it was new and recently noticed thing. It is not, people have been aware of the issues related to childlings for years. That, and the way you focus on that aspect and the language you use regarding it is presenting the issue as if it was a common thing in Changeling.<br /> <br /> This is not the case, remember that most Changeling players are used to taking stuff they like and ignoring the rest. Or dealing with conflicting rules vs lore the setting presents. Any online game with CtD will be chock full of houserules, almost on princible. So any loli sex goddess would be houseruled away before it would even cross anyone's mind.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And that's a good thing... why exactly? If I need to houserule the entire game to make it work, then why did I buy the book in the first place? Make-believe is 100% free.<br /> I mean, the core problem here is that &quot;fairies as a metaphor for sex&quot; and &quot;fairies as a metaphor for childhood&quot; don't belong in the same game. The game with adult matters and sex magic in it (and CtD has sex magic other than Gift of Pan) <i>should not</i> have &quot;3-13 y.o. child&quot; as one of its core character generation choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T14:02:28-08:00","id":803346,"title":"","content":"...fairies aren't a metaphor for sex. They're not a metaphor at all. They're just what you are.<br /> <br /> The game tends to be heavily about coming of age.<br /> <br /> That sex and childhood are both themes in a game with that focus, and which is designed to focus on various parts of the whole process of growing up, should be no surprise. That you assume because both are present, they MUST be conflated...well, that's not the game's fault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T14:08:37-08:00","id":803348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/800734-sell-me-on-changeling?p=803344#post803344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And that's a good thing... why exactly? If I need to houserule the entire game to make it work, then why did I buy the book in the first place? Make-believe is 100% free.<br /> I mean, the core problem here is that &amp;quot;fairies as a metaphor for sex&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;fairies as a metaphor for childhood&amp;quot; don't belong in the same game. The game with adult matters and sex magic in it (and CtD has sex magic other than Gift of Pan) <i>should not</i> have &amp;quot;3-13 y.o. child&amp;quot; as one of its core character generation choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like we need to trigger warning this entire thread now, which has been derailed from its original subject to... well... this...<br /> <br /> It's not a good thing that we have to houserule, which is why we're happy for a C20. However, the point is, no one who isn't a disturbed sex monster plays loli sex goddesses. It's something that people have noticed, but it's not as if the game even suggests it as a valid character type. It's just an unfortunate side effect of bad wording and writers naively (but understandably) not expecting players to have an obsession with loli sex goddesses (I feel like someone's getting royalties every time we say this?).<br /> <br /> Point me to one sample character or NPC that is a loli sex goddess? It's not there in the text. It's a possible character type, if you're a pervert, but then any roleplaying game can be abused if people really want to indulge their underage sex fantasies.<br /> <br /> It should be obvious that playing such a character is revolting. If it isn't, then it's the player we need to have words with, not anyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T14:33:30-08:00","id":803359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/800734-sell-me-on-changeling?p=803344#post803344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And that's a good thing... why exactly? If I need to houserule the entire game to make it work, then why did I buy the book in the first place? Make-believe is 100% free.<br /> I mean, the core problem here is that &quot;fairies as a metaphor for sex&quot; and &quot;fairies as a metaphor for childhood&quot; don't belong in the same game. The game with adult matters and sex magic in it (and CtD has sex magic other than Gift of Pan) <i>should not</i> have &quot;3-13 y.o. child&quot; as one of its core character generation choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe\">adambeyoncelowe's </a></b>great post, because what the game promises and presents IS interesting and complex. That is what attracted so many to CtD in the first place, and that's why people have been playing the game, with house rules, for so long. Because the idea it presents and the potential stories it tells are worth it. That should tell why Changeling is worth checking out, if the players have stuck with the idea of this game, despite its massive flaws, there has to be something there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T14:41:03-08:00","id":803364,"title":"","content":"I don't get it. Why are we discussing about something that is clearly a problem with someone and not with the game mechanics? Condemn CtD for this fault is the same to condemn every single RPG (or games in general) that doesn't actually spend all their efforts policing every opportunity to be misunderstood and corrupted.<br /> Let the creeps with their creepy thoughts inside their heads (aka don't feed the trolls).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T15:01:03-08:00","id":803376,"title":"","content":"Now, the other kind of trolls (the blue ones), they're another reason to play the game! I mean, who doesn't want to be a seven-foot tall honorable warrior?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T20:12:55-08:00","id":803519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally poste